#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_failure

#% text
# `is_failure(x)` gives `true` if `x` is a failure `failure(tag, ...)`, and `false` otherwise.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A failure is the value a computation gives when it cannot produce a result: its tag says why (`no_match`, `argument`, `not_converged`, `missing_key`, ...).

#% item
# Failures pass through most functions unchanged, so a failure deep in a computation becomes its value. `is_failure` is one of the few functions that receive the failure as an argument instead.

#% item
# A list that contains a failure is not itself a failure; `drop_failures` removes such elements from a list.

#% item
# `failure_tag(x)` gives the tag.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
is_failure(failure(not_found, "key"))
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_failure(42)
#% output
#= false

#% cell
is_failure(lookup(assoc(), "k"))
#% output
#= true

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The failures of numerical functions:

#% cell
is_failure(find_root(x^2 + 1, [x, 1]))
#% output
#= true

#% cell
failure_tag(find_root(x^2 + 1, [x, 1]))
#% output
#= not_converged

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# Counting the failed points of a scan; the list keeps its failures as elements:

#% cell
results = map(a => find_root(x^2 - a, [x, 1]), [4, -1, 9])
count_if(results, is_failure)
#% output
#= 1

#% text
# A fallback when a computation fails:

#% cell
fn root_or_missing(a) = if is_failure(find_root(x^2 - a, [x, 1])) then missing("no root") else x /. find_root(x^2 - a, [x, 1])
map(root_or_missing, [4, -1])
#% output
#= [2.0, missing("no root")]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# A list holding a failure is not a failure:

#% cell
is_failure([1, failure(a, f)])
#% output
#= false

#% text
# `drop_failures` removes failed elements from a list:

#% cell
drop_failures(results)
#% output
#= [[x -> 2.0], [x -> 3.0]]

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# A failure is not stored by an assignment: the failure is the value of the statement and the name stays unassigned, so test the computation itself, not a name it was assigned to:

#% cell
r = find_root(x^2 + 1, [x, 1])

#% cell
is_failure(r)
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `failure_tag`, `drop_failures`, `find_root`, `lookup`
